      "rationale": "PMID: 41677647 explicitly states that statins inhibit the HMGCR-dependent activation of the mevalonate pathway."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Statin-induced inhibition of HMGCR can modulate the NUPR1-mediated insulin signaling axis in cancer cells.",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "rationale": "PMID: 41677647 discusses statins inhibiting HMGCR and downregulating NUPR1, which impairs IR-mediated signaling."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Statin exposure can trigger immune-mediated necrotizing myopathy (IMNM) through the development of anti-HMGCR antibodies.",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "rationale": "PMID: 41200259 describes IMNM associated with statin exposure and anti-HMGCR antibodies."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Bioinformatics analyses suggest that the modulation of the cholesterol-metabolism pathway may have potential protective roles in chronic respiratory diseases.",
